title:: Keyboard Shortcuts
summary:: Keyboard shortcuts for SuperCollider
categories:: Frontends

note:: For shortcuts bindings of teletype::ScIDE::, please consult the menu and/or the shortcut configuration menu.::

section:: Vim Keybindings in ScIDE

ScIDE includes an optional Vim-style modal editing mode. This is separate from the external teletype::scvim:: editor integration listed in the tables below. Enable it from menu::Preferences > Editor > Behavior > Enable Vim keybindings::. It is disabled by default.

When enabled, the status bar shows the current mode: teletype::NORMAL::, teletype::INSERT::, teletype::VISUAL::, or teletype::VISUAL LINE::. During a search it instead shows the active teletype::/:: or teletype::?:: prompt. The cursor is narrow in Insert mode and character-width in the other modes. Vim commands use an unnamed register and last-search pattern shared by all ScIDE editor panes. The standard platform copy, cut, and paste shortcuts continue to use the system clipboard.

subsection:: Modes and insertion

table::
## strong::Key:: || strong::Action::
## teletype::i:: || enter Insert mode at the cursor
## teletype::I:: || enter Insert mode at the start of the line
## teletype::a:: || enter Insert mode after the cursor
## teletype::A:: || enter Insert mode at the end of the line
## teletype::o:: || open a line below and enter Insert mode
## teletype::O:: || open a line above and enter Insert mode
## teletype::v:: || enter or leave characterwise Visual mode
## teletype::V:: || enter or leave linewise Visual mode
## teletype::Esc:: || return to Normal mode and cancel pending commands
::

subsection:: Motions

These motions work in Normal and Visual modes and may follow the teletype::d::, teletype::c::, or teletype::y:: operators. A decimal count repeats a motion or command; operator and motion counts multiply, as in teletype::2d3w::.

table::
## strong::Key:: || strong::Action::
## teletype::h:: / teletype::l:: || move one character left / right
## teletype::j:: / teletype::k:: || move one line down / up
## teletype::w:: / teletype::b:: || move to the next / previous word
## teletype::e:: || move to the end of the word
## teletype::W:: / teletype::B:: / teletype::E:: || move by whitespace-delimited WORDs
## teletype::0:: || move to the start of the line
## teletype::^:: || move to the first non-whitespace character
## teletype::$:: || move to the end of the line
## teletype::gg:: / teletype::G:: || move to the start / end of the document
## teletype::f{char}:: / teletype::F{char}:: || move to the next / previous character on the line
## teletype::t{char}:: / teletype::T{char}:: || move just before / after that character
## teletype::;:: / teletype::,:: || repeat the last character motion forward / in reverse
## teletype::%:: || move to the matching parenthesis, bracket, or brace
::

subsection:: Search

Search patterns use case-sensitive Qt regular-expression syntax and wrap at document boundaries. The match is previewed while the pattern is typed. Press teletype::Return:: to accept the search or teletype::Esc:: to restore the original cursor position.

table::
## strong::Key:: || strong::Action::
## teletype::/:: / teletype::?:: || search forward / backward
## teletype::n:: / teletype::N:: || repeat the last search in the same / opposite direction
## teletype::*:: / teletype::#:: || search forward / backward for the word under the cursor
::

subsection:: Text objects

Text objects may follow teletype::d::, teletype::c::, or teletype::y::, or be used from characterwise Visual mode.

table::
## strong::Key:: || strong::Action::
## teletype::iw:: / teletype::aw:: || inner word / word including surrounding whitespace
## teletype::i(:: / teletype::a(:: || inside / around the enclosing parentheses
## teletype::i[:: / teletype::a[:: || inside / around the enclosing brackets
## teletype::i{:: / teletype::a{:: || inside / around the enclosing braces
## teletype::i":: / teletype::a":: || inside / around double quotes on the current line
## teletype::i':: / teletype::a':: || inside / around single quotes on the current line
::

subsection:: Editing

table::
## strong::Key:: || strong::Action::
## teletype::x:: || delete the character under the cursor
## teletype::X:: || delete the character before the cursor
## teletype::s:: / teletype::S:: || substitute characters / whole lines and enter Insert mode
## teletype::r{char}:: || replace characters without entering Insert mode
## teletype::~:: || toggle character case and advance
## teletype::J:: || join lines
## teletype::>>:: / teletype::<<:: / teletype::==:: || indent / unindent / reindent lines
## teletype::d{motion}:: || delete through a supported motion
## teletype::c{motion}:: || change through a supported motion and enter Insert mode
## teletype::y{motion}:: || yank through a supported motion
## teletype::dd:: / teletype::D:: || delete the current line / to the end of the line
## teletype::cc:: / teletype::C:: || change the current line / to the end of the line
## teletype::yy:: / teletype::Y:: || yank the current line
## teletype::p:: / teletype::P:: || paste after / before the cursor or line
## teletype::u:: / teletype::Ctrl-R:: || undo / redo
## teletype::.:: || repeat the last Normal-mode document change
## teletype::d::, teletype::x::, teletype::c::, teletype::y::, teletype::p:: || apply the operation to the Visual selection
::

Modified ScIDE shortcuts remain active while Vim mode is enabled, including code evaluation, completion, document, and navigation shortcuts. Marks, named registers, macros, command-line and substitution commands, configurable mappings, and blockwise Visual mode are not currently implemented. Searches are navigation commands and cannot currently be used as operator motions.

